WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:16.517
Unit eleven: Verb + -ing vs Infinitive. Today you will choose between -ing and to + verb after common verbs.

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:19.376
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:23.775
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:26.071
Enjoy + -ing.

7
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:30.360
Enjoy + -ing means a verb pattern with the -ing form.

8
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.241
I enjoy swimming.

9
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.083
Your turn. Say: Enjoy + -ing.

10
00:00:38.933 --> 00:00:40.724
Enjoy + -ing.

11
00:00:41.483 --> 00:00:42.705
Want + to.

12
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:47.121
Want + to means a verb pattern with the infinitive.

13
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:48.857
I want to travel.

14
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.009
Your turn. Say: Want + to.

15
00:00:54.867 --> 00:00:56.355
Want + to.

16
00:00:57.117 --> 00:00:57.944
Gerund.

17
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.389
Gerund means the -ing form of a verb used as a noun.

18
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:04.484
Swimming is a gerund.

19
00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:07.294
Your turn. Say: Gerund.

20
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.018
Gerund.

21
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:12.924
Infinitive.

22
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.880
Infinitive means to + the base form of a verb.

23
00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:19.274
To travel is the infinitive.

24
00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:22.234
Your turn. Say: Infinitive.

25
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.194
Infinitive.

26
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:27.603
Like.

27
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.638
Like means to enjoy; it can take both patterns.

28
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.820
I like reading or to read.

29
00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:36.605
Your turn. Say: Like.

30
00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.131
Like.

31
00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:41.792
Decide.

32
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:46.002
Decide means to choose; followed by to + verb.

33
00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:48.105
She decided to study.

34
00:01:48.717 --> 00:01:51.392
Your turn. Say: Decide.

35
00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.200
Decide.

36
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.905
Avoid.

37
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:01.344
Avoid means to stay away from; followed by -ing.

38
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.508
Avoid making noise.

39
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:06.932
Your turn. Say: Avoid.

40
00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:10.675
Avoid.

41
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:12.104
Hope.

42
00:02:13.117 --> 00:02:17.717
Hope means to want and expect something; followed by to + verb.

43
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:19.666
I hope to pass.

44
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.624
Your turn. Say: Hope.

45
00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:25.910
Hope.

46
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.548
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:34.497
Visal, do we say 'I enjoy to swim' or 'I enjoy swimming'?

48
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:51.590
I enjoy swimming. Some verbs are followed by the -ing form: enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, mind. Others are followed by to + verb: want, decide, hope, plan, need.

49
00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:53.719
And like?

50
00:02:54.817 --> 00:03:07.282
Like, love and hate can take both patterns with little change in meaning: I like reading. I like to read. But after would like we always use to: I would like to read.

51
00:03:08.383 --> 00:03:09.918
How can I remember?

52
00:03:11.017 --> 00:03:26.195
Learn verbs in groups. Enjoy, avoid, finish + -ing. Want, decide, hope, plan + to. Make your own examples: I decided to study. I finished studying. Practice makes it natural.

53
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:28.903
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:35.500
Grammar focus: Verb patterns: verb plus -ing and verb plus to plus base verb.

55
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.079
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.527
I enjoy swimming in the river.

57
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:42.080
I want to travel next year.

58
00:03:42.983 --> 00:03:44.913
She decided to study medicine.

59
00:03:45.867 --> 00:03:54.350
Enjoy, avoid, finish + -ing. Want, decide, hope, plan, need + to + base verb. Like, love and hate can take both.

60
00:03:55.083 --> 00:03:58.363
Be careful! Don't say: I enjoy to swim.

61
00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.974
Say: I enjoy swimming.

62
00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:03.821
Use -ing after enjoy.

63
00:04:04.633 --> 00:04:07.146
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:07.933 --> 00:04:09.445
Choosing the Right Pattern.

65
00:04:09.745 --> 00:04:12.186
I enjoy swimming and I want to learn diving.

66
00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.092
She decided to study medicine, so she avoids wasting time.

67
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.411
We hope to travel next year, and we plan to save money.

68
00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.038
He finished doing his homework and started to cook.

69
00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.277
A verb followed by -ing is a gerund.

70
00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:33.693
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:35.818
I enjoy blank.

72
00:04:36.118 --> 00:04:39.237
A, to read. B, reading. C, read.

73
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.382
The answer is B: reading.

74
00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:47.133
She wants blank a doctor.

75
00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:50.529
A, to be. B, being. C, be.

76
00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:55.822
The answer is A: to be.

77
00:04:56.983 --> 00:04:58.809
They decided blank early.

78
00:04:59.109 --> 00:05:02.484
A, leaving. B, to leave. C, leave.

79
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.859
The answer is B: to leave.

80
00:05:09.017 --> 00:05:10.633
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:10.933 --> 00:05:16.177
A, He avoids to go.. B, He avoids going.. C, He avoids go..

82
00:05:19.733 --> 00:05:22.244
The answer is B: He avoids going..

83
00:05:23.383 --> 00:05:26.254
According to the reading, what do they plan to do?

84
00:05:26.554 --> 00:05:30.985
A, save money. B, learn diving. C, cook dinner.

85
00:05:34.533 --> 00:05:36.382
The answer is A: save money.

86
00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:40.962
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:41.817 --> 00:05:45.639
Write one sentence with a verb followed by -ing and one with an infinitive.

88
00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.857
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:56.157 --> 00:06:09.752
I enjoy reading in the evening. I want to improve my English. I use enjoy + -ing and want + to + base verb. These two patterns are different, so I must learn which verbs take which form.

90
00:06:10.052 --> 00:06:11.773
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:19.678
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb patterns: verb plus -ing and verb plus to plus base verb.

92
00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:24.348
Today's value is lifelong learning. Keep learning for as long as you live.

93
00:06:24.648 --> 00:06:27.173
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

94
00:06:27.473 --> 00:06:30.590
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

